\f0\fs24 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 These data include a subset of single-cell samples from the CPTAC Renal Cell Carcinoma data processed using the following steps:\uc0\u8232 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Loom
\f0\i0  files were read into R and converted into 
\f1\i SingleCellExperiment
\f0\i0  objects.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ensembl gene ID's were matched to HGNC symbols, chromosome name, starting position, and ending position via Biomart using the 
\f1\i scater
\f0\i0  R package.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Size factors were computed using the 
\f1\i scran
\f0\i0  R package.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 UMAP dimensions were computed using the 
\f1\i scater
\f0\i0  R package.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Probes without matching HGNC symbols were removed.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Where duplicate HGNC symbols were present, the gene with the maximum normalized range was retained.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cell types were inferred using the 
\f1\i scMRMA
\f0\i0 \'a0R package.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cells with less than or equal to 1,000 features were removed.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cells with mitochondrial reads greater than or equal to 50% were removed.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Expression data for podocytes and macrophages were saved separately for each sample.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	11	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For podocytes and macrophages for each sample, expression data were projected onto the first 100 principal components using the 
\f1\i irlba
\f0\i0  R package.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	12	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For macrophages for each sample, a differentiation trajectory was estimated using the 
\f1\i monocle3
\f0\i0  R package, and plots were colored by combined expression of the M0 markers CSF1R, CD14, CD68, and CD11B, the M1 markers CD86, MARC0, CXCL9, CXCL10, CXCL11, NOS2, SOCS1, and CD64, and the M2 markers TGM2, CD23, ARG1, CCL22, CD163, and CD206 (from PMC8268869). Pseudotime starting points were annotated in 
\f1\i monocle3
\f0\i0  using visual inspection of plots. Only samples in which a visible trajectory from M0 -> M1 -> M2 was evident using these markers were retained.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	13	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For podocytes for each sample, a differentiation trajectory was estimated using the 
\f1\i monocle3
\f0\i0  R package, and plots were colored by combined expression of the dedifferentiation markers DACH1 (from PMC5908116) and PTPRO (from PMID9639039. Pseudotime starting points were annotated in 
\f1\i monocle3
\f0\i0  using visual inspection of plots. Only samples in which a visible trajectory of dedifferentiation was evident using these markers were retained.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls14\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	14	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For podocytes and macrophages for each sample, 10-fold cross-validation matrices for expression, PCA, and pseudotime were generated across 5 random splits, for a total of 50 files per cell type, per sample.\
